    "evidence": "Root cause / primary sink exercised: dolphinscheduler-common/src/main/java/org/apache/dolphinscheduler/common/utils/HadoopUtils.java `mkdir`/`getHdfsFileName` (line ~549 format, sink `new Path(...)` at HadoopUtils.java:280 inside `mkdir`), reached from ResourcesServiceImpl.createDirectory (build fullName at line 140 from unsanitized `currentDir` + validated `name`, private createDirectory() at line ~600-609 calling HadoopUtils.getHdfsFileName then HadoopUtils.getInstance().mkdir(directoryName)). Trust boundary: `currentDir` is an attacker-supplied HTTP request parameter (ResourcesController -> ResourcesService.createDirectory/createResource/onlineCreateResource) that reaches Hadoop filesystem path construction with no traversal validation, while only the co-located `name`/`fileName` parameter is checked via FileUtils.directoryTraversal(name). Confirmed by direct source inspection: `currentDir` never passed to FileUtils.directoryTraversal (or any equivalent check) in the current baseline at ResourcesServiceImpl.java lines 140, 217, and 973. Every distinct sink/path a complete fix must guard, per the alert: (1) createDirectory: currentDir/name -> fullName (line 140) -> HadoopUtils.getHdfsFileName -> HadoopUtils.mkdir -> new Path (HadoopUtils.java:280) [POV target]; (2) createDirectory delete-on-conflict path: fullName -> getHdfsFileName -> directoryName -> HadoopUtils delete (ResourcesServiceImpl.java ~600-609); (3) createResource/updateResource: name -> fullName (line 217/335) -> destHdfsFileName via getHdfsFileName -> HadoopUtils.copy -> new Path (HadoopUtils.java:293-294, ResourcesServiceImpl.java ~489-493); (4) onlineCreateResource: fileSuffix/name/currentDir -> fullName (line 973) -> uploadContentToHdfs -> getHdfsResourceFileName -> HadoopUtils dstHdfsPath -> new Path (HadoopUtils.java:308-312, ResourcesServiceImpl.java ~1099-1127), reachable both via the fileSuffix/name chain and the currentDir chain (two traces in the alert's 3rd vulnerability group); (5) rename/move path: name -> fullName (line 217/307/335) -> hdfsFilename via getHdfsFileName -> HadoopUtils dstHdfsPath -> new Path (HadoopUtils.java:308-312, ResourcesServiceImpl.java ~628-651), reachable via two separate entry traces (create-then-rename and direct name chains).",
